Arm the frame dump and the GPU capture from a file, not only from F12.

Ctrl+Shift+D and F12 need a hand on the keyboard, and the game under Wine
does not always have one: a scripted run, a headless comparison, or a
session driven from a remote shell has no way to press anything. This adds
a second trigger — touch `/tmp/mtld3d_dump` or `/tmp/mtld3d_capture` and
the next frame is dumped or captured, exactly as a keypress would.

Applies to `reference/mtld3d` before `tools/mtld3d_build.sh`. Its companion
patches are `mtld3d_frame_dump_geom.patch` and
`mtld3d_frame_dump_constants.patch`; the three are independent and can go
on in any order.

